y Calendar","description":null}}},"chat_info":{"conversation_id":"89ffae50-7ee6-49af-ba4b-35ceb6a3f5f8","turn_id":"9348ee45-7512-4943-81bc-dbbb3a53923a","user_ui_message_id":"cde621ab-e707-4b5d-9ac4-8de66bd11478","assistant_ui_message_id":"cc5a8f76-21e1-4557-8266-180017d32573"}}','{"X-Family-ID":"09a097f6-d708-49e4-8ccf-a78cab898ba0","X-Timezone":"Asia/Shanghai","X-User-ID":"a7a2dfb9-0995-489a-929e-88be06e1bf2f","TraceId":"dsafsdfasdf"}','[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Suggestions for dinner"}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Looking for some dinner ideas for you!"},{"type":"tool_call","tool_call":{"id":"SWCxYbaShVVST7Lj","name":"recipe_searchRecipes","arguments":{"query":"dinner"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_result":{"name":"recipe_searchRecipes","content":"[{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-0552fd3f-9016-466f-8adc-89e208cb70bd\",\"name\":\"Shabu Shabu Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":30,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Place an electric wok or electric skillet in the center of the table.;2. Arrange meat, seafood, vegetables, and tofu on platters.;3. Place cooked rice in a serving bowl and set it on the table.;4. Set out bowls of pickles.;5. Set each diner''s place with a plate, chopsticks (or forks for the timid), a rice bowl, a small plate for pickles, and individual bowls of dipping sauces.;6. Bring broth and kombu (if using) to a simmer in the wok or skillet.;7. Remove and discard kombu if used.;8. Allow diners to select and cook their own meat and vegetables in the simmering broth using their chopsticks or forks.;9. At the conclusion of dinner, pour any remaining broth into bowls and pass them around the table.\",\"ingredients\":\"Shabu shabu or sukiyaki meat: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Sea scallops: piece 18 , is_optional: ;Prawns: piece 12 , is_optional: ;Shiitake mushrooms: piece 12 , is_optional: ;Napa cabbage: head 0.5 , is_optional: ;Green onions: piece 12 , is_optional: ;Bamboo shoots: can 1 , is_optional: ;Leaf spinach: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Firm tofu: oz 12 , is_optional: ;Short-grain rice: cup 2 , is_optional: ;Pickled vegetables:   , is_optional: ;Dipping sauces:  1 , is_optional: ;Chicken broth: cup 4 , is_optional: ;Kombu (kelp): piece 1 , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":2},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-9a30dbbc-a3d2-4273-9fb5-856faee70761\",\"name\":\"Pasta Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":35,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. At 6:15 PM, set out appetizers (Grapes, Wine, Breadsticks) on the coffee table.;2. At 6:15 PM, start preparing the Focaccia Bread Mix.;3. At 6:20 PM, preheat the oven for the focaccia and start water boiling for the pasta.;4. At 6:30 PM, start cooking the focaccia and pasta, aiming for them to finish at roughly the same time.;5. At 6:40 PM, combine the Onion & Garlic Tomato Sauce and Fried Meatballs, then microwave for 5 minutes.;6. Combine the cooked Medium Shell Pasta, heated sauce, and meatballs in a large pasta bowl.;7. Empty the bag of salad into a large bowl.;8. Set out the focaccia on a large plate.;9. Empty croutons into a small bowl.;10. Set out salad dressing.;11. Pour drinks (Coke, Lemonade, Wine).;12. Serve and enjoy!\",\"ingredients\":\"Grapes:  1 , is_optional: ;Wine: bottle 1 , is_optional: ;Breadsticks: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Fried Meatballs: batch 1 , is_optional: ;Onion & Garlic Tomato Sauce: jar 1 , is_optional: ;Pappa''s Focaccia Bread Mix: pk 2 , is_optional: ;Salad: bag 1 , is_optional: ;Coke: bottle 1 , is_optional: ;Croutons: pk 1 , is_optional: ;Lemonade: bottle 1 , is_optional: ;Salad dressing: bottle 1 , is_optional: ;Medium Shell Pasta: lb 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":2},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-46a3b36a-6442-4978-8d27-178c863af682\",\"name\":\"Beef and Barley Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":60,\"servings\":5,\"instructions\":\"1. In a 4-quart saucepan or Dutch oven, brown ground beef.;2. Add green pepper, onion, and garlic.;3. Cook until onion is tender; drain.;4. Add remaining ingredients (water, canned tomatoes, tomato paste, barley, sugar, salt).;5. Bring to a boil.;6. Reduce heat to low; cover.;7. Simmer 45 to 50 minutes or until barley is tender, stirring occasionally.\",\"ingredients\":\"Lean ground beef: lb 1 , is_optional: ;green pepper: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;onion: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;garlic clove: clove 1 , is_optional: ;water: cup 2.5 , is_optional: ;canned tomatoes: oz 16 , is_optional: ;tomato paste: oz 6 , is_optional: ;QUAKER Barley: cup 0.75 , is_optional: ;sugar: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;salt: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":1},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-14a931c3-6623-4a0f-8a2f-6bbcca1ac942\",\"name\":\"Chicken Dinola\",\"cooking_time\":60,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Peel the papaya skin. Cut papaya lengthwise into 4-6 pieces, remove seeds, and slice diagonally about 1/2 inch thick. Set aside.;2. In a deep soup pot over medium heat, saute garlic in oil until lightly browned.;3. Add ginger and onion, stir for a minute.;4. Add chicken pieces and fish sauce. Cook for 3 minutes.;5. Add water. Season with a little salt and pepper. Let boil, then simmer covered over medium-low heat for 25-30 minutes.;6. Add raw papaya (or potatoes, if substituting) and continue cooking for 6 to 8 minutes or until tender.;7. Correct seasonings to taste. Turn off heat.;8. Add spinach, cover for 1-2 minutes.;9. Serve immediately.\",\"ingredients\":\"chicken: lb 2 , is_optional: ;garlic: clove 2 , is_optional: ;vegetable oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;fresh ginger: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;onion:  1 , is_optional: ;fish sauce: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;water: cup 4.5 , is_optional: ;raw green papaya:  1 , is_optional: ;salt:   , is_optional: ;black pepper:   , is_optional: ;fresh spinach: bunch 1 , is_optional: ;potatoes:  2 , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-b73f2e94-cc09-4065-84f7-ae5a8c17addc\",\"name\":\"Skillet Mac Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":30,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Brown the ground meat with the onion, garlic, and celery.;2. Drain off any excess fat.;3. Add mushrooms and corn and stir to cook briefly.;4. Add chili powder, cumin, and the dried red chili peppers (crushing them). Then add tomato soup, water, sugar, and ketchup.;5. When this mixture is hot and bubbly, add the drained cooked macaroni.;6. Gently stir to coat the macaroni with the sauce.;7. Serve hot in big bowls.\",\"ingredients\":\"ground meat: lb 1 , is_optional: ;onion:  0.5 , is_optional: ;celery: stalk 2 , is_optional: ;mushrooms: piece 6 , is_optional: ;corn: can 1 , is_optional: ;garlic: clove 2 , is_optional: ;tomato soup: can 1 , is_optional: ;water: can 0.5 , is_optional: ;chili powder: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;cumin: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;sugar: cup 0.125 , is_optional: ;dried red chili peppers:  2 , is_optional: is optional;ketchup: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;macaroni: cup 3 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-5284118a-6d2e-4fee-b63e-9b9352bd031d\",\"name\":\"Curly Noodle Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":15,\"servings\":3,\"instructions\":\"1. Brown the ground beef; drain off any excess fat.;2. Stir in the ramen noodles (unopened), their seasoning packet, stewed tomatoes, and drained corn.;3. Bring the mixture to a boil, then reduce heat and simmer until the noodles are done.\",\"ingredients\":\"ground beef: lb 1 , is_optional: ;beef flavored ramen noodles: packet 1 , is_optional: ;stewed tomatoes: can 1 , is_optional: ;kernel corn: can 1 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-42fa96cf-0d0a-4f47-b180-a1d6c2c4032a\",\"name\":\"Pot Roast Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":25,\"servings\":6,\"instructions\":\"1. Trim fat from roast. If necessary, cut roast to fit into crock pot.;2. In a skillet, brown roast on all sides in hot oil.;3. In a bowl, combine tomato juice, vinegar, worcestershire sauce, sugar, salt, basil, thyme, pepper, and garlic.;4. In a 6 quart crockpot, place carrots and onions.;5. Sprinkle tapioca over vegetables.;6. Place browned roast atop vegetables.;7. Pour tomato mixture over roast.;8. Cover and cook on low-heat setting for 10-12 hours or high-heat for 5-6 hours.;9. Transfer meat and vegetables to a platter.;10. Skim fat from gravy.;11. Serve gravy with mashed potatoes.\",\"ingredients\":\"beef chuck roast: lb 3 , is_optional: ;oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;tomato juice: cup 1.5 , is_optional: ;red wine vinegar: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;worcestershire sauce: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;sugar: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;salt: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;basil: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;thyme: tsp 0.5 , is_optional: ;pepper: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;garlic clove:  1 , is_optional: ;carrots:  6 , is_optional: ;boiling onions:  6 , is_optional: ;tapioca: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;mashed potatoes:  6 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":1},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-53960c41-5076-444a-a503-151dbd958eec\",\"name\":\"Spaghetti Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":18,\"servings\":1,\"instructions\":\"1. Crumble ground beef into a 1-quart microwave-safe casserole; add onion.;2. Microwave on high for 2 - 2 1/2 minutes or until no longer pink; stirring once.;3. Drain; stir to break meat into smaller pieces.;4. Add tomato sauce, water, and spaghetti.;5. Cover with casserole lid.;6. Microwave 10 - 11 minutes or until spaghetti is tender, stirring twice.;7. Serve with Parmesan Cheese.\",\"ingredients\":\"Ground beef: lb 0.25 , is_optional: ;Chopped onion: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Italian seasoned tomato sauce: can 1 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Spaghetti: oz 2.5 , is_optional: ;Parmesan cheese:   , is_optional: is optional\",\"reference_count\":3},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-f5a4fa12-04d0-45e5-a9dc-bea653734fac\",\"name\":\"Omelet and Noodle Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":45,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Heat 1 teaspoon of oil in a wok or skillet over high heat until nearly smoking. Add bean sprouts, celery, and snow peas. Cook, stirring constantly, for 1 minute and immediately transfer the cooked vegetables to a work bowl.;2. To the work bowl with vegetables, add scallions, diced ham, and 2 tablespoons of soy sauce. Sprinkle in cornstarch and mix well.;3. Add beaten eggs and 1/4 cup of water to the vegetable mixture and mix thoroughly. Set this egg mixture aside.;4. Cook the Chinese noodles for 5 minutes in boiling salted water. Drain and set aside.;5. In a soup pot, combine dark sesame oil, minced garlic, and minced ginger. Place over low heat and cook for 1 minute.;6. Add red pepper flakes, low-sodium chicken broth, bottled clam juice, 3 tablespoons of soy sauce, rice or white vinegar, and dry sherry to the soup pot. Cover, increase heat to medium, and boil for 5 minutes.;7. Heat frying oil (about 3/8-inch depth) in a large skillet over high heat. Add 3-ounce ladles of the egg mixture to form omelets. Cook until edges puff, about 1 minute, then flip and cook on the other side for about 30 seconds.;8. Remove cooked omelets and drain them on paper towels. Cover and keep warm while preparing the remaining omelets.;9. When ready to serve, divide the cooked noodles and broth between 4 soup bowls.;10. Make a bed of shredded iceberg lettuce in each bowl.;11. Arrange the omelets on top of the lettuce.;12. Garnish with fresh cilantro and serve.\",\"ingredients\":\"Frying oil: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Bean sprouts: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Celery stalks: stalk 2 , is_optional: ;Snow peas: piece 8 , is_optional: ;scallions: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Diced ham: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Soy sauce: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Cornstarch: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Eggs:  9 , is_optional: ;Water: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Fresh Chinese noodles: lb 0.5 , is_optional: ;Dark sesame oil: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Minced garlic: tbsp 1 , is_optional: ;Minced ginger: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;Red pepper flakes: tsp 0.25 , is_optional: ;Low-sodium chicken broth: cup 2 , is_optional: ;Bottled clam juice: cup 1 , is_optional: ;Soy sauce: tbsp 3 , is_optional: ;Rice or white vinegar: tbsp 2 , is_optional: ;Dry sherry: cup 0.25 , is_optional: ;Shredded iceberg lettuce: cup 2 , is_optional: ;Cilantro:  0 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0},{\"id\":\"c06f7d7-73da11f1-40a2-4dff-bf2a-cd7396b755bb\",\"name\":\"Norwich Inn Boiled Chicken Dinner\",\"cooking_time\":20,\"servings\":4,\"instructions\":\"1. Spray a 4-5 qt nonstick saucepot with vegetable cooking spray and place over moderate heat.;2. Sauté boned and skinned chicken breasts until lightly browned on both sides.;3. Add dry white wine, crushed garlic, leeks (white part only, washed and cut into 1-inch slices), and celery (cut into 1-inch slices). Cook for 5 minutes.;4. Add carrots (cut into 1-inch slices), cored cabbage (cut into 8 wedges), medium size potatoes, tomatoes, caraway seeds, tarragon (fresh or dried substitute), bay leaf, and chicken broth (preferably reduced sodium and defatted).;5. Bring the mixture to a boil over high heat.;6. Reduce heat to low, cover, and cook until vegetables are tender, about 30 minutes.;7. Spoon chicken and vegetables into heated soup plates with some of the broth.;8. Sprinkle with parsley before serving.\",\"ingredients\":\"Chicken breast: half 4 , is_optional: ;Dry white wine: cup 0.5 , is_optional: ;Garlic: clove 2 , is_optional: ;Leeks:  2 , is_optional: ;Celery: stalk 3 , is_optional: ;Carrots:  2 , is_optional: ;Green cabbage:  0.5 , is_optional: ;Potatoes:  4 , is_optional: ;Tomatoes:  2 , is_optional: ;Caraway seeds: tsp 1 , is_optional: ;Tarragon: tsp 2 , is_optional: ;Bay leaf:  1 , is_optional: ;Chicken broth: oz 14.5 , is_optional: ;Vegetable cooking spray:  0 , is_optional: ;Parsley:  0 , is_optional: \",\"reference_count\":0}]","success":true,"tool_call_id":"SWCxYbaShVVST7Lj"}}]},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here are some dinner suggestions for you:\n\n*   **Shabu Shabu Dinner**: A delightful and interactive meal with a cooking time of 30 minutes, perfect for a cozy family gathering.\n*   **Pasta Dinner**: A classic and satisfying meal that takes about 35 minutes to prepare, featuring pasta with